📝 Common Git Commands
  
| Command        | Description                     |
| -------------- | ------------------------------- |
| `git init`     | Initialize a new Git repository |
| `git clone`    | Copy a repository               |
| `git add`      | Stage files for commit          |
| `git commit`   | Save changes with a message     |
| `git branch`   | Create or list branches         |
| `git checkout` | Switch branches                 |
| `git merge`    | Combine branches                |
| `git push`     | Upload code to remote           |
| `git pull`     | Download code from remote       |


🌿 Git Branching Strategy Example
Creating a Repository with Three Branches

# 1. Initialize git
git init

# 2. Connect to GitHub repository (public)
git remote add origin https://github.com/username/repo-name.git

# 3. Make main branch and push abstraction file
git branch -M main
git add .
git commit -m "Added abstraction application in main branch"
git push -u origin main

# 4. Create second branch (subset of main)
git checkout -b branch-two
git add .
git commit -m "Extended abstraction application"
git push -u origin branch-two

# 5. Create third branch (separate)
git checkout main
git checkout -b branch-three
git add .
git commit -m "Separate abstraction application"
git push -u origin branch-three
